course: dictionary
lesson: 11179
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word wipe is one of them. Its most common meaning is to rub something with a cloth, tissue or your hand to clean or dry it. «Wipe your nose with a tissue» tells you to clean your nose.
explain: The words around wipe show you which meaning to use. «Wipe up the spill so nobody slips» means clean up the wet mess on the floor, because the spill and the slipping are clues. To wipe out means to destroy something completely, so «Whaling nearly wiped out some species» means whaling almost destroyed some kinds of whale.
explain: Use the same check as always: ask what fits, then try your meaning in the sentence. If you think wipe means rub, does «Wipe your feet before you come in» still make sense? It does, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Wipe can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). A wipe is a small damp cloth used for cleaning.
fact: «Wipe your feet» means rub your shoes clean before you go inside.
fact: «Wipe out» means destroy completely, as in «wiped out some species».
fact: «Wipe a device» means delete everything on it, as in computing.
fact: The same word can have different meanings: to wipe a table means to clean it, but to wipe a file means to delete it.
exercise: «Wipe your feet before you come in.» What does wipe mean here? | To wash the whole house | *To rub your shoes clean on a mat | To paint the front door | To jump over the doorstep
exercise: «Whaling nearly wiped out some species.» What does wiped out mean here? | Cleaned very carefully | *Destroyed completely | Left behind for a short time | Painted over in bright colours
exercise: Mia packed baby wipes in her bag. What is a wipe? | A loud noise | *A small damp cloth for cleaning | A kind of shoe | A type of bird
test: «Wipe up the spill so nobody slips.» Why do you wipe up the spill? | To make a loud splash | To wipe the words off the board | *To stop someone slipping on the wet floor | To make the floor shiny for a party
test: Sam says, «Before I sold the old tablet, I wiped everything on it.» What does wiped mean in computing? | Cleaned the screen gently | Dried it in the sun | *Deleted everything on it | Charged it fully
exam: «Having changed does not wipe out responsibility for what you did before.» What does wipe out mean here? | Make it bigger | *Cancel or erase completely | Say it loudly | Write it down
